# Paths vibecheck skips when scanning its own repository.
#
# Everything here is insecure on purpose. Nothing here is a suppression of a
# real problem — if you find yourself adding a line to hide a genuine finding,
# fix the finding instead.

# The guides and the landing page quote vulnerable code so that readers can
# recognise it in their own projects. Flagging our own worked examples would
# be a long joke at our expense.
guides/
index.html

# tests/ used to be listed here. It no longer needs to be: findings in test
# paths are demoted to info automatically, because nothing in a test file
# ships. One fewer suppression to trust.

# rules.py is a table of vulnerability descriptions, so its prose matches its
# own patterns — "subprocess is called with shell=True" is a fix prompt, not a
# subprocess call. Only this one data file is excluded; every module with
# actual logic in it is still scanned.
vibecheck/rules.py
